  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording from May 4, 2005, captures Mountain Goats performing at the First Unitarian Church in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania [1][2]. The setlist includes fifteen songs plus an encore, beginning with “Lions Teeth” and concluding with “Jenny” [1]. Notable tracks include “Blue Jays and Cardinals,” which is the first in the archive and considered mythic rare due to only two archived performances [1][2]. The band also performed “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent,” “California Song,” and “Quito” [1]. The recording was taped and transferred by Thomas J Hartnett, who noted it was the first show he ever recorded [1]. He mentioned a skip at the beginning of “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent” caused by accidentally pulling the mic cord, which he edited using Audacity [1]. The performance lasted approximately 61 minutes [1]. This is show 68 of 467 in the archive’s collection for the performer [2]. The previous archived show was on April 28, 2005, at Will’s Pub [2]. The recommended recording is the only available one, featuring all 16 songs [1].",
